    {
      "after": {
        "bytes": 7136,
        "git_blob": "85430163e07a9ac5d0b8d226f3c3947ee08d19f0",
        "mode": "100644",
        "sha256": "3e6c49491020f417f8dbeb79e9aaec348096ca2bcecbf6b797f60bb399571b3d",
        "text": "# Explicit Linux file roundtrip cold and portable qualification\n\nThis owner selects `hepta.hia.linux-file-roundtrip.v2` explicitly. It does not\nactivate a default CLI, enlarge the original worker resource profile, or claim\nwhole-language/native qualification. The installed static ELF executes without\na Python interpreter or libc. Python remains the author, cold-build supervisor,\ntest observer before `execve`, independent VM/reference provider, and auditor.\n\n## Source and compiler authority\n\n`tools/build_hia_linux_file_roundtrip_cold.py` admits the actual current-source\ncold replay, its complete nested qualification, all three B1/B2/B3 image bytes,\ntheir original receipts, and the current complete source manifest. It adds its\nown explicit source closure and the five versioned optional resources. A\ndevelopment compiler pin, old successful report, or serialized fixture alone\ncannot grant this admission. Every public admission repeats fresh checks.\n\nThe build uses actual current cold B3 to compile the process profile P1, then P2\nand P3. All three compiled images must match. P3 must compile the ordinary\nselfhost source back to the exact admitted cold B3 bytes. P3 then compiles the\ncontroller, private representation resident, semantic resident and ELF packer.\nThe actual HIA packer produces the aggregate ELF; its complete payload extents\nand bytes are checked by the existing structural inspector. No resident is\nsubstituted with a saved development image.\n\nEvery original compilation keeps its 20-second child bound and 1 MiB output\nand workspace. Each actual request, original child stdout/stderr, receipt,\ncomplete output buffer and produced image is retained and read back. The ELF\nalso must fit the original 1 MiB bound. Nothing in this owner changes the B3\n128-function, 1536-block or 8192-operation limits.\n\n`--portable` additionally publishes the real compiled ELF with mode 0500 and\nthe exact five resource bytes in a separate bundle. The bundle manifest is an\ninstallation record; requalification still requires fresh original cold\nadmission. The ELF itself needs no bundle-loading Python at execution time.\n\n## Fixed permanent groups\n\nRun the complete qualifier from a matching source checkout:\n\n```text\npython -B tools/qualify_hia_linux_file_roundtrip.py --cold-report <actual-cold-report> --evidence <new-directory>\n```\n\nThe four groups have new permanent unittest identities. The original inputs,\norder, return codes, complete stdout/stderr and assertions remain fixed in\n`tests/fixtures/hia_linux_file_roundtrip_retained.zlib.json`. Its exact wrapper\nand decompressed identities are pinned by the custody owner.\n\n| Group | Methods | Required observations |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Kernel | 130 | Every original input in order; actual static ELF return, complete stdout/stderr, unchanged input and ELF, timeout and cleanup |\n| Pipeline | 7 | Original complete VM input/provider/error behavior; all three buffers under 10 million steps; six actual kernel whole-buffer comparisons |\n| Tail faults | 2 | Exact C1 or C2 last-byte injection; unchanged length/full-equality guard; actual native and VM code 72/phase 7, no stdout, three complete buffers |\n| Portable | 1 | Actual sdist, default and explicitly selected wheels, install, cold-built bundle, three actual installed ELF executions, resource/ELF drift refusals |\n\nEach group and preparation keep a separate original 180-second process owner\nand 3-second cleanup. Every VM has the original 10-million-step limit. Each\ndirect kernel observer keeps its original 20-second wall/3-second cleanup and\noriginal CPU/address/stack/file/descriptor limits. The extra packaging commands\nhave a 60-second subprocess bound inside the unchanged 180+3 group owner.\n\nThe six full native F/O/W observations are written by the separately compiled\npure HIA postreturn observer. It contains exactly the actual production\ncontroller and resident bytes. Its test-only startup writes the actual BSS\nthrough file descriptors 29, 30 and 31 after the controller returns. Python\nopens those output descriptors before `execve`; it does not construct or edit\nthe observed buffers. The extents are 8,388,609, 1,048,576 and 1,048,576 bytes.\nThe seventh pipeline row is explicitly VM-only for the original read-error\nplus close-error priority case. It is not assigned an invented native result.\n\nThe qualifier re-reads every original exec request, stdout/stderr, actual\npostreturn file, VM frame, compile observation, start/stop event and cleanup\nreceipt. It requires exact loaded/started/stopped ID order and all methods.\nSkips, expected failures, unexpected successes, subtest failures, partial\nreports, changed inputs and boolean substitutes for integer counts all refuse\nqualification. Ordinary group failures retain later fixed groups; actual source\ndrift stops further execution. Failure reports and all files are retained.\n\n## Installation and original worker resources\n\nThe default wheel continues to contain the original 210 worker resources:\nNATIVE92 and ENTRY19 remain unchanged. This owner adds no HIA asset to those\nroles. The independent profile registry supplies the already existing five\nroundtrip assets. A selected wheel is built only with:\n\n```text\nHEPTA_HIA_BUILD_PROFILES=hepta.hia.linux-file-roundtrip.v2\n```\n\nThe portable group builds both the ordinary 210-resource wheel and the\nexplicitly selected 215-resource wheel, using no package index or wheel cache.\nIt checks every resource and every installed Python source byte. The executable\nis copied from the admitted actual cold build, read back, kept 0500 and executed\nfrom the installed bundle. Missing resources, changed source bytes and a\nchanged ELF last byte are refused before payload execution. These tests are\nexplicit-profile observations, not permission to use an ambient source tree.\n\n## Qualification boundaries and preserved failures\n\nThe original roundtrip pipeline7 succeeded in its own development experiment.\nThe separately frozen semantic resident R5 suite has six logical VM controls:\nfive passed and `root-v8-cross-target-loans` exhausted the unchanged 10-million\nstep budget. That failure remains explicit in every fixture and qualification\nreport. The pipeline seven and checker six are different fixed groups. A pass\nhere does not turn the separate failure into a pass and does not claim complete\nsemantic-resident VM qualification.\n\nThe profile uses bounded internal JSON/node/function/attribute domains. An\n8 MiB file-read buffer is not a claim that the full 8 MiB external grammar is\naccepted. The private representation resident accepts its three exact internal\nmagics; it is not a compatibility replacement for the two public canonical\nentry magics. The original public representation assets remain separate.\n\nAt initial authoring of this successor, no new cold positive, Native, portable,\nor CPython 3.14 qualification has been executed. The Source class checks fixed\ninputs, original code projection, registration, strict refusal and evidence\nmechanics only. Historical reports and source packages are retained as\nhistorical evidence, never transferred to the new source generation.\n"
      },
      "before": null,
