    },
    {
      "after": {
        "bytes": 7050,
        "git_blob": "6a42683b78127d8e89f15a442f755eb57f8e16ad",
        "mode": "100644",
        "sha256": "03dcf48f78f322561aa162f3975f7be3a66d63cbd104680b8717b5240f2096c0",
        "text": "# Explicit native VerifiedProgram report owner\n\nThis component executes all seven retained `VerifiedProgram` representation\nand report method bodies as HIA continuations. It adds an optional sixth image\nto the existing CLI parser, formatter, discovery JSON, discovery routing and\nparser-context bundle. The original default CLI remains available and is not\nselected by this component.\n\nThe selected CLI's original effect 9 first evaluates its real `.report`\nattribute. An exact definition-time bound method on the original slotted class\ncan enter the HIA report owner. Changed class descriptors, code, attribute hooks\nand foreign callables use their actual original operations. The result is an\nordinary live Python dictionary. Verification, decoding, hashes, schema and\nfeature providers remain actual mutable providers; this owner grants no new\nverification authority.\n\n## Portable selection\n\n`tools/build_hia_cli_verified_report_bundle.py` preserves the original five\ncomponent directories, manifests, requests, receipts and `build.json`. It\nadds `verified_report/`, `verified-report-build.json` and the explicitly\nselectable `verified-report-bundle.json`. The outer bundle keeps every original\ncompanion field and adds the report manifest identity. The existing\n`HEPTA_HIA_CLI_MANIFEST` selection recognizes only this exact new schema.\n\n`installed_cli` retains admitted immutable code while freshly binding source\nand manifest bytes. `installed_cli_strict` also reads every current image.\nInstalled source resolution uses the existing closed package-resource rule;\nauthoring tools are not runtime dependencies. The actual original 43 caller\ntests, including the built wheel and installed subprocess, remain byte exact.\n\n## Explicit build authority\n\nProduction construction requires a real matching-current-source cold replay.\nThe custody chain re-admits its original 180-second qualification and 3-second\ncleanup owner, the real B1/B2/B3 fixed point, all current source digests, and\nthe six actual compile requests, complete child stdout/stderr, receipts and\nfull 1 MiB outputs. Every compile retains its 20-second limit. The ordinary\ndevelopment B3 is available only through an explicitly labelled development\nbuild and cannot be admitted as a cold fixture.\n\n```\npython -B tools/build_hia_cli_verified_report_bundle.py \\\n  --output NEW_BUILD --compiler CAPTURED_B3 --cold-report CURRENT_COLD\npython -B tools/qualify_hia_cli_verified_report_bundle.py \\\n  --cold-report CURRENT_COLD --evidence NEW_QUALIFICATION\n```\n\nThe qualifier requires the complete original 43 ordered test IDs, the permanent\nmethod containing all 140 retained report and CLI observations, and a separate\nactual image-drift control for warm mappings and strict image readback.\nPreparation and each group retain separate 180+3 supervision. Skips, expected\nfailures, missing IDs, boolean counters, changed source and incomplete cleanup\nare rejected. Their observation reports never grant cold authority themselves.\n\nThe first seven-file development component passed 140 actual CPython 3.14.4\ncomparisons and recorded 35,747 real machine frames. That historical result\ndoes not qualify this portable successor or its current-source cold path.\nNew preparation and test outcomes must be recorded independently. This is not\na complete native verifier, standalone CLI executable, or closure of the\nthirteen file actions and their publication effects.\n# Versioned optional resource origin (v2)\n\nThe v2 report component and six-image bundle use\n`hepta.hia.verified-report-native.v2` and\n`hepta.hia.cli-verified-report-bundle.v2`. The preceding v1 source, manifests,\nobservations and failures remain historical evidence; their hashes are not\nrenamed into v2 qualification.\n\nThe default Agent installation retains the original twelve resource roles:\n19 entry assets, 92 native bridge assets, and 210 resources in total. Its Python\nsource identity still includes newly installed Python modules. The optional\nregistry therefore does not promise an unchanged whole worker digest.\n\nThe independent `hepta.hia_optional_profiles` registry names exact versioned\nprofiles and source byte identities. A normal wheel installs the default 210\nresources. Explicit `HEPTA_HIA_BUILD_PROFILES` selects comma-separated profile\nidentifiers for additional wheel resources under `hepta/_data`; unknown,\nduplicate, missing, symlinked or changed resources reject the build. An sdist\nretains all eight optional source assets. No product module is imported to\ndiscover packaging resources, and resource presence never chooses a profile.\n\nThe report builder captures the actual current-source report HIA bytes inside\nits explicit bundle. The component manifest declares `profile_resources`,\nincluding `source_root`, the complete relative source path, its SHA-256, the\nfixed profile identity, and installed host compatibility identities. The loader\nuses that declared bundle origin exclusively. It verifies the fixed source pin,\nthe independent host/ports compatibility anchor, safe paths, and complete\nmanifest/resource bytes before and after mapping. Missing bundle data never\nfalls back to package resources, a checkout, cwd or HOME. Explicit profile-wheel\ninstallation is a separate supported source origin and is checked independently.\n\nThe original 43 CLI test byte streams and ordered IDs remain unchanged. Their\nfixture provider still constructs the complete six-image report bundle. Their\nexisting bundle copy carries the declared report source; their temporary source\nproject and default wheel remain at the original 210 resources. No test name,\nmissing file or partial fixture triggers an implicit resource copy or fallback.\n\nThis authoring revision has no current-source cold positive until its actual\nstrict qualifier runs against a matching complete cold report. Development\ncompilation and packaging controls do not supply that qualification. Compile\n20 s, 1 MiB buffers, 10 M VM fuel and original group 180+3 s remain unchanged.\n\n# Optional resource capture successor\n\nThe explicit v2 bundle uses the bytes returned by `fresh_profile_capture`,\nincluding its captured report HIA source, instead of checking a path and then\nopening it again. Each read holds the complete root and directory descriptor\nchain, opens the final file with `O_NOFOLLOW | O_NONBLOCK`, requires a regular\nfile of the declared bounded extent, and checks the descriptor and named\nbindings before returning. The twelve actual host source files use the same\ncapture; eleven still have a separate fixed compatibility anchor, while the\nregistry is included in current-source cold custody.\n\nThe report builder and qualifier consume those actual captures. The optional\nsetup branch copies captured bytes and publishes them through a held output\ndirectory; the default worker's twelve roles and 210 resources are unchanged.\nThe inherited five-image loader and general cold producer are outside this\nfilesystem-race repair. No matching-current-source cold or whole CLI\nqualification follows from authoring or Source controls alone.\n\n"
      },
      "before": null,
      "path": "docs/HIA_VERIFIED_REPORT_NATIVE.md"
    },
